 **Steps:**
-
-1. **Partition the Interval Tree:**
-   Partition the nodes of the interval tree such that each region fits into one disk block. Assume one disk block stores at most $2^{K_1+1}-1$ interval tree nodes in a binary subtree of depth $K_1$ [S1, unofficial].
-
-2. **Label Tree Nodes:**
-   Label tree nodes $\eta$ to determine block boundaries using the following recursive definition [S1, unofficial]:
-   $$
-   \ell(\eta) := 
-   \begin{cases} 
-   K_1 & \text{if } \eta \text{ is a leaf} \\
-   \ell_0(\eta) & \text{if } \eta \text{ is not a leaf and not the root} \\
-   0 & \text{if } \eta \text{ is the root}
-   \end{cases}
-   $$
